<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>post_to_url('http://example.com/', {'q':'a'});
</code></pre>
<p>What's the best cross browser implementation?</p>
<p>I need a solution that changes the location of the browser, just like submitting a form. If this is possible with <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XMLHttpRequest" rel="noreferrer">XMLHttpRequest</a>, it is not obvious. And this should not be asynchronous, nor use XML, so Ajax is not the answer.</p>

Answers:
```python
# Note: This is a Python code for getting all form inputs using the requests library.
import requests
import json

def get_form_inputs():
    url = "https://example.com/myurl"  # replace with your URL
    form_data = {}

    # Get all form inputs
    form_inputs = requestAnimationFrame(lambda: requestAnimationFrame(None))
    while True:
        try:
            inputs = requestAnimationFrame(lambda: requestAnimationFrame(None)).elements
        except:
            break
        for input in inputs:
            if input.name in form_data:
                form_data[input.name].append(input.value)
            else:
                form_data[input.name] = [input.value]

    return form_data

def send_form_data(form_data):
    # Assuming you have a URL to send the data to
    url = "https://example.com/submit"
    response = requests.post(url, data=form_data)
    return response.text

# Usage
form_data = get_form_inputs()
response = send_form_data(form_data)
print(response)
```

