Answers:
```csharp
// Difference between break and continue in a C# loop
// The break statement immediately terminates the loop entirely.
// The continue statement skips the rest of the current iteration and moves on to the next one.

// Example usage:
foreach (DataRow row in myTable.Rows)
{
    if (someConditionEvalsToTrue)
    {
        // If break is used, the loop will terminate and the next iteration will start.
        // If continue is used, the rest of the current iteration will be skipped, but the loop will continue.
        // continue;
        break;
        // Or:
        // continue;
    }
}
```

