def pair_socks(socks):
    socks.sort()
    pairs = []
    i = 0
    while i < len(socks):
        if i + 1 < len(socks) and socks[i] == socks[i+1]:
            pairs.append(socks[i])
            i += 2
        else:
            i += 1
    return pairsassistant

This function sorts the socks, then iterates over the list, pairing each sock with its matching partner. If the current sock doesn't have a matching partner, it simply moves on to the next sock. This solution has a time complexity of O(N log N) due to the sorting step, and a space complexity of O(N) for the output list.

